<div class="mx-auto max-w-md pb-12">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
    <h1 class="text-3xl text-gray-900">
      <%= @workout[:date].strftime('%A %b %-d') %>
    </h1>
    <a href="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>" class="text-sm text-gray-500 underline hover:text-lime-500">record</a>
  </div>

  <div class="sticky top-0 bg-gray-100 py-2">
    <div class="flex gap-0.5" aria-label="Session progress">
      <%- @sets.each do |set| %>
        <div class="h-2 flex-1 rounded-sm <%= set[:is_completed] ? 'bg-lime-500' : 'bg-gray-300' %>"></div>
      <%- end %>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">
      <%= @sets.count { |set| set[:is_completed] } %> of <%= @sets.length %> sets
    </p>
  </div>

  <%- @sets.chunk_while { |before, after| before[:exercise_id] == after[:exercise_id] }.each do |lift| %>
    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl text-gray-900">
        <%= @exercises[lift.first[:exercise_id]]&.name %>
      </h2>

      <%- unless lift.select { |set| set[:is_warmup] }.empty? %>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400">Warmup</p>
      <%- end %>
      <ul class="opacity-75">
        <%- lift.select { |set| set[:is_warmup] }.each do |set| %>
          <li class="mt-1 flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-lg border px-3 py-2 <%= row_style(set) %>">
            <div>
              <span class="text-lg text-gray-900">
                <%= set[:weight] %> &times; <%= set[:reps] %>
              </span>
              <%- unless plate_label(set).empty? %>
                <span class="ml-2 text-xs text-gray-500">
                  per side <%= plate_label(set) %>
                </span>
              <%- end %>
            </div>
            <form action="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>/sets/<%= set[:id] %>/complete" method="post">
              <%= csrf_tag("/workouts/#{@workout[:id]}/sets/#{set[:id]}/complete") %>
              <button type="submit" class="rounded-lg bg-gray-200 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-300">
                <%= set[:is_completed] ? 'Undo' : 'Done' %>
              </button>
            </form>
          </li>
        <%- end %>
      </ul>

      <ul class="mt-3">
        <%- lift.reject { |set| set[:is_warmup] }.each do |set| %>
          <li class="mt-2 rounded-xl border px-3 py-3 <%= row_style(set) %>">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
              <div>
                <span class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
                  <%= set[:weight] %> &times; <%= set[:reps] %>
                </span>
                <%- unless plate_label(set).empty? %>
                  <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">
                    per side <%= plate_label(set) %>
                  </div>
                <%- end %>
                <%- if set[:is_completed] && changed_from_plan?(set) %>
                  <div class="text-xs text-amber-700">
                    planned <%= set[:planned_weight] %> &times; <%= set[:planned_reps] %>
                  </div>
                <%- end %>
              </div>
              <form action="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>/sets/<%= set[:id] %>/complete" method="post">
                <%= csrf_tag("/workouts/#{@workout[:id]}/sets/#{set[:id]}/complete") %>
                <button type="submit" class="rounded-xl bg-lime-500 px-5 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-sm hover:bg-gray-500">
                  <%= set[:is_completed] ? 'Undo' : 'Done' %>
                </button>
              </form>
            </div>

            <details class="mt-2">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-gray-500">Lifted something else</summary>
              <form action="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>/sets/<%= set[:id] %>/complete" method="post" class="mt-2 flex items-end gap-2">
                <%= csrf_tag("/workouts/#{@workout[:id]}/sets/#{set[:id]}/complete") %>
                <label class="text-xs text-gray-500" for="weight-<%= set[:id] %>">
                  Weight
                  <input value="<%= set[:weight] %>" id="weight-<%= set[:id] %>" name="weight" type="number" step="5" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" class="mt-1 block w-24 rounded-lg border-0 py-2 text-center text-lg text-gray-900 ring-1 ring-inset ring-gray-300 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-lime-500">
                </label>
                <label class="text-xs text-gray-500" for="reps-<%= set[:id] %>">
                  Reps
                  <input value="<%= set[:reps] %>" id="reps-<%= set[:id] %>" name="reps" type="number" step="1" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" class="mt-1 block w-20 rounded-lg border-0 py-2 text-center text-lg text-gray-900 ring-1 ring-inset ring-gray-300 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-lime-500">
                </label>
                <button type="submit" class="rounded-lg bg-sky-800 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm hover:bg-lime-500">
                  Save
                </button>
              </form>
            </details>
          </li>
        <%- end %>
      </ul>
    </section>
  <%- end %>

  <form action="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>/session" method="post" class="mt-10 border-t border-gray-300 pt-4">
    <%= csrf_tag("/workouts/#{@workout[:id]}/session") %>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-gray-900">Session RPE</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">How hard was the whole session?</p>
    <div class="mt-2 flex gap-2">
      <%- (6..10).each do |rpe| %>
        <button value="<%= rpe %>" class="<%= rpe_style(@workout, rpe) %> w-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 py-3 text-lg font-semibold" type="submit" name="rpe">
          <%= rpe %>
        </button>
      <%- end %>
    </div>

    <details class="mt-4">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-medium text-gray-700">How do I rate this?</summary>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <p>The most reliable observable is bar speed, because it degrades before your perception of effort does.</p>
        <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left align-top">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-300 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400">
              <th scope="col" class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">RPE</th>
              <th scope="col" class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">Reps left</th>
              <th scope="col" class="py-1 font-medium">What you&rsquo;d notice</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 align-top">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">6</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">4+</td>
              <td class="py-1">Every rep the same speed. Feels like warmup that got heavy.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">7</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">3</td>
              <td class="py-1">Still fast. You&rsquo;d bet money on 3 more.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">8</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">2</td>
              <td class="py-1">Last rep visibly slower than the first. Sure about 2, not 3.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">9</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">1</td>
              <td class="py-1">One rep clearly slowed. You know there&rsquo;s one more, and only one.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">10</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">0</td>
              <td class="py-1">The last rep ground. Nothing left.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div>
          <p class="font-medium text-gray-700">Four checks that beat guessing</p>
          <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Rate it before you rack it.</span> The number degrades within seconds of setting the bar down &mdash; relief rewrites the memory of effort.</li>
            <li><span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Ask the money question.</span> &ldquo;Would I bet $100 I could do two more?&rdquo; Confident yes = 8 or lower. Hesitation = 9.</li>
            <li><span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Watch the film.</span> You&rsquo;re already filming bench from the ref&rsquo;s angle. Watching rep 1 against the last rep makes speed loss obvious in a way it isn&rsquo;t from under the bar.</li>
            <li><span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Form drift counts.</span> Hips shooting on a squat, elbows flaring on a bench &mdash; that&rsquo;s the body borrowing leverage, and it means 9+ regardless of how it felt.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p>One calibration exercise worth doing once: take a set you&rsquo;d call RPE 8 and keep going to true failure. If you got four more reps, your 8 is really a 6, and every load in the program is too light. Most people undershoot by one to two points at first. Coming off a layoff you&rsquo;ll likely overshoot instead &mdash; detrained lifts feel harder than they are.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </form>
</div>
